The goldens are this port's output. TWO of the five still differ from the
reference dazzle, and both differ for ONE reason — they were re-checked against
/usr/local/bin/dazzle while the goldens were blessed, and the port's side is
identical with the arena ON, with it OFF, and on the commit before either
landed.

  useloss  the reference additionally reports two ArcEngine diagnostics
           ("reference in architecture to non-existent ID").
  noparts  same cause: the reference adds "element DSSSL-SPECIFICATION
           unfinished in meta-DTD".

Both come from the VALIDATING half of the architecture engine, which is not
ported: the port keeps the architecture as a GATE (see the file header of
dazzle/DssslSpecEventHandler.scaly), so nothing ever validates the
architectural instance against the meta-DTD. Measured 2026-08-09:
opensp/ArcEngineMessages.scaly has 40 accessors and ZERO callers. Recorded as
an open item in COMPLETENESS.md — do not "fix" these two goldens without that
engine.

  extspec  ✅ no longer deviates (2026-08-09). The missingPart anchor of a
           SPECID reference read the event's `loc` (past the GI name) where the
           reference builds the StartElementEvent with markupLocation(); it now
           reads markup_loc and the fixture is character-identical.

Everything these fixtures are FOR — that the location survives its parse and
still resolves to the right file, line and column — is identical to the
reference in all five, and extok (a runtime error resolving through an external
specification's chunk table into an entity-expanded .scm) is character-for-
character equal.
